      "message": "iff (old, new) is one of:\n        ('new', 'paid'), ('new', 'cancelled'), ('paid', 'refunded')\n    Any other pair -> False.\n\"\"\"\n\nCONTRACT_VERSION = 2\n\nALLOWED_TRANSITIONS = frozenset({\n    ('new', 'paid'),\n    ('new', 'cancelled'),\n    ('paid', 'refunded'),\n})\n\ndef can_transition(old, new):\n    \"\"\"Return True iff the (old -> new) status transition is permitted in v2.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return (old, new) in ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS\n    except TypeError:  # unhashable inputs can never match the table\n        return False\n```\n\n`can_transition('paid', 'refunded')` returns `True`; all non-listed pairs (`'refunded'->'paid'`, `'paid'->'cancelled'`, `'paid'->'paid'`, `None->'paid'`) return `False`.\n\n**To finish:** the write path needs to be fixed on your side (the attempt directory doesn't exist at the resolved root and `run_command` is refusing all commands). Once writes land, re-run me or drop the block above into `A_direct_attempt_2/producer.py` \u2014 it is self-contained and needs no further edits."
